fetcher
  1. fetches the flag configuration once per request with its source version
     expected: a fetch without a previous version returns the flag configuration and a non-empty source version
  2. reports not changed when given the current source version, and never without one
     expected: a fetch given the current source version reports Unchanged, and a fetch without a previous version never does
  3. returns a new source version after the source changed
     expected: after the source changed, a fetch given "v0" returns the changed flag configuration with a new source version
  4. abandons a running fetch when its context is done
     expected: a fetch with a done context returns within 300ms
  5. reports a failed fetch without returning a flag configuration
     expected: a fetch of a broken source returns an error and no flag configuration
fetch trigger
  1. signals only for the change signal, so it never fetches or delivers on its own
     expected: no signal in the 300ms before the change signal arrives
  2. signals each time the change signal arrives
     expected: one signal for each arrival of the change signal, here two
  3. reconnects after losing the change signal
     expected: a signal for a change signal that arrives after the connection was lost
  4. returns nil from Run on shutdown
     expected: Run returns nil within 300ms of the context being done
  5. stops listening on shutdown
     expected: no signal for a change signal that arrives after shutdown
streaming sync provider
  1. stays up when the source is unavailable at startup and delivers once it answers
     expected: the provider stays up and not ready while the source is unavailable, then delivers and is ready
  2. delivers the source's complete flag configuration first
     expected: the complete flag configuration within 300ms
  3. delivers the flag configuration unchanged
     expected: the delivered flag configuration equals {"flags":{"one":{}}}
  4. reports readiness
     expected: IsReady is true within 300ms of the first delivery
  5. delivers each change the source pushes
     expected: a delivery of the changed flag configuration
  6. delivers the complete flag configuration again on request
     expected: ReSync returns nil and delivers the complete flag configuration, {"flags":{"two":{}}}
  7. reconnects after losing the source
     expected: after the source was lost and came back, a delivery of the complete flag configuration, {"flags":{"two":{}}}
  8. delivers what its source's removal calls for
     expected: a removed source delivers nothing (Keep): the last accepted flags stay in force
  9. stops on shutdown
     expected: Sync returns nil within 300ms of the context being done
  10. names its source
     expected: every delivery names the configured source "stub://flags"
